WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.150
Two waves.

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.110
Three sine x, with peaks three high.

3
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.330
And four cos x, with peaks four high.

4
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.440
Now add their heights, point by
point, to build a third curve.

5
00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.680
It's one smooth wave,
with the same period.

6
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:19.450
But its peaks don't reach seven: the
two waves never peak at the same x.

7
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.790
So how tall is the new wave?

8
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.280
Could it be the average, three and a half?

9
00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:29.140
In this mission, you'll use the compound
angle formula to expand sine of A plus

10
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.060
B.

11
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.870
You'll compare coefficients of
sine and cosine on each side.

12
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.200
And you'll write any mix of sine and
cosine as a single wave, shifted sideways.

13
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: work out how
tall the new wave will be.
